{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/923565-some-confusion-on-indomitable","id":923565,"title":"Some Confusion on Indomitable","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-29T16:40:06-07:00","id":923565,"title":"Some Confusion on Indomitable","content":"Hey all, I'm a little confused on how the Indomitable merit works with Disciplines like Majesty and Nightmare, specifically the tiers like Awe and Dread Presence that have no cost and no roll, and just start affecting everyone in the area. I'm pretty sure Indomitable should defend against these, but I'm not clear how it would do so. I think it's pretty reasonable that the +2 from Indomitable should apply to the Wits + Composure roll to notice anyone else with Awe, but that doesn't really change the fact that your emotions and thoughts have already been manipulated.<br /> <br /> The only thing I can think of is the Lashing Out bit, but it's specifically related to vampires. Is it sensible to allow a Mortal to 'Lash Out' using the same rules for Predatory Aura, and then just give the bonus to that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T17:03:10-07:00","id":923574,"title":"","content":"Those effects are just cosmetic enough that I don't resent the impossibility to resist them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T17:06:11-07:00","id":923575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/923565-some-confusion-on-indomitable?p=923574#post923574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those effects are just cosmetic enough that I don't resent the impossibility to resist them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't seem too cosmetic when they allow you to ignore social penalties and take a bonus to social rolls through emotional manipulation, Especially when Werewolves and Mages still have to overcome that merit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 06-29-2016, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T17:14:49-07:00","id":923579,"title":"","content":"I've actually got another question as well, but it doesn't seem right making another thread over it. In the Blood Sympathy section it states that Once Removed is &quot;For Sires and their Childer exclusively.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does this mean that the Close Family merit does not boost Twice Removed family members to Once Removed status?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T18:39:35-07:00","id":923614,"title":"","content":"Indomitable could add to the dice pool to resist Presence rolls by a user of Majesty, as the Discipline adds Majesty dots to their Presence rolls. You might add it to the Wits + Composure rolls involved as well. Dread Presence would allow the same, as a user 'adds her Nightmare dots to all mundane Intimidate rolls.' Those rolls are supernaturally charged and now you can resist them with Indomitable.<br /> <br /> As for Close Family, no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> D<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">oes this mean that the Close Family merit does not boost Twice Removed family members to Once Removed status?</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">That's not what the Merit does. </span>'As well, treat all relations as one step closer for the purposes of sympathy distances.' Only the sympathy range limits would be boosted.<br /> <br /> It's worth keeping in mind, though, that just because one game has to deal with something doesn't mean others do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T19:51:34-07:00","id":923646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/923565-some-confusion-on-indomitable?p=923614#post923614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indomitable could add to the dice pool to resist Presence rolls by a user of Majesty, as the Discipline adds Majesty dots to their Presence rolls. You might add it to the Wits + Composure rolls involved as well. Dread Presence would allow the same, as a user 'adds her Nightmare dots to all mundane Intimidate rolls.' Those rolls are supernaturally charged and now you can resist them with Indomitable.<br /> <br /> As for Close Family, no.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">That's not what the Merit does. </span>'As well, treat all relations as one step closer for the purposes of sympathy distances.' Only the sympathy range limits would be boosted.<br /> <br /> It's worth keeping in mind, though, that just because one game has to deal with something doesn't mean others do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you, this response helped a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:57:44-07:00","id":924003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/923565-some-confusion-on-indomitable?p=923614#post923614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indomitable could add to the dice pool to resist Presence rolls by a user of Majesty, as the Discipline adds Majesty dots to their Presence rolls. You might add it to the Wits + Composure rolls involved as well. Dread Presence would allow the same, as a user 'adds her Nightmare dots to all mundane Intimidate rolls.' Those rolls are supernaturally charged and now you can resist them with Indomitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that your Indomitable would kick in when the Awe/Dread Presence user tries to persuade/intimidate you. When they roll, you roll, until then they dont really influence you to do or feel anything major so that merit wouldnt really help. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T06:07:25-07:00","id":924414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/923565-some-confusion-on-indomitable?p=923575#post923575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially when Werewolves and Mages still have to overcome that merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only insofar as their powers are contested or resisted, as this is what Indomitable adds to. A Cahalith using Voice of Glory Auspice Gift is as undeterred by Indomitable as a Daeva using Awe.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, mages don't really give a fuck about Indomitable in 2e, as supernal magic is withstood rather than contested or resisted, and Indomitable does nothing for Withstanding as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":582,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","user":"Morangias","date":". 07-01-2016, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T06:49:08-07:00","id":924428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/923565-some-confusion-on-indomitable?p=924414#post924414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Actually, mages don't really give a fuck about Indomitable in 2e, as supernal magic is withstood rather than contested or resisted, and Indomitable does nothing for Withstanding as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Any time a supernatural creature uses a power to influence your character's thoughts or emotions, add a +2 die bonus to the dice pool to contest it. If the roll is resisted, instead subtract a -2 die penalty from the monster's die pool.'<br /> <br /> Indomitable would likely cause the second effect, since Withstanding is a form of resistance, not contesting. Nothing says a Withstood rating can't be altered by Merits, and that's specifically what Merits and other special abilities are for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T07:20:04-07:00","id":924436,"title":"","content":"Contesting and resisting are both system terms, as is Withstanding. The Merit adds to the former two, it does nothing about the latter.<br /> <br /> Merits do what they say they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T07:38:12-07:00","id":924444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/923565-some-confusion-on-indomitable?p=924436#post924436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Merits do what they say they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. And any time a supernatural power to influence a character's thoughts or emotions is resisted, a -2 die penalty is subtracted from the monster's die pool.<br /> <br /> Actually the developer commented on this, and said, 'Because a Withstand level is the equivalent of a Potency, which is a two-die penalty to the caster to account for, our advice when judging how penalty-based powers work is to halve the penalty; in that spirit, Indomitable would be +1.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-01-2016, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}